## Implementation plan

### TDD approach (Red-Green-Refactor)

The implementation follows Test-Driven Development principles to ensure quality and prevent regressions.

### Phase 1: Write tests that identify the problem (RED)

**Goal:** Prove that the problem exists by writing tests that fail.

- [ ] Create test file: `[path].test.tsx`
- [ ] Write at least one failing test per acceptance criterion above
- [ ] Run the tests and verify that they fail (RED)

**Details:**
```tsx
// Example test that should fail
test('should [description]', () => {
  // Arrange
  // Act
  // Assert - should fail because functionality is missing
});
```

### Phase 2: Implement the solution (GREEN)

**Goal:** Implement minimal code to make the tests pass.

- [ ] Implement changes in `[file1.tsx]`
- [ ] Implement changes in `[file2.tsx]`
- [ ] Run tests and verify that they pass (GREEN)

**Details:**
[Description of the implementation with code examples]

### Phase 3: Verify that the tests pass (GREEN)

- [ ] Run unit tests: `<project test command> [filename]`
- [ ] Run integration tests if relevant
